.TH COF-INFO 1 "2026-11-13" "cof 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cof-info \- Show details for a bundled orchestration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
cof info [OPTIONS] {name}
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows a bundled orchestration's own details from the curated index:
description, category, complexity, and required extensions.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B name
NAME Name of the orchestration.
.TP
.B --json
Output machine-readable JSON only.
.TP
.B --config, -c
CONFIG Path to config JSON (or use CIRCUITRY_CONFIG).
.TP
.B --profile
PROFILE Named profile to layer in when resolving the complexity block, as `cof
run --profile` would (see `cof run --help`).
.TP
.B --scoring, --no-scoring
Preview runtime.complexity.scoring forced on/off, as `cof run --scoring` would
resolve it.
.TP
.B --routing, --no-routing
Preview runtime.complexity.routing forced on/off, as `cof run --routing` would
resolve it.
.TP
.B --decompose, --no-decompose
Preview runtime.complexity.decomposition forced on/off, as `cof run
--decompose` would resolve it.
.TP
.B --split, --no-split
Preview runtime.complexity.splitting forced on/off, as `cof run --split` would
resolve it.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B cof info hello-world
Shows one bundled orchestration's details.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The command failed, or the input was invalid.
.TP
.B 2
A usage error -- an unrecognized option or missing argument.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBcof(1)\fR, \fBcof-list(1)\fR, \fBcof-eject(1)\fR
